## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest                  # unit tests for every module + an integration test
python -m {{ package }}  # run the smoke simulation
```

No install needed for a first look: `pytest` works from the project root.

## Architecture

- **{{ spec.subsystems | length }} subsystems, {{ spec.module_count }} modules, {{ spec.topics | length }} topics, {{ spec.messages | length }} message types.**
- Modules never import each other. They exchange immutable, typed messages over
  `core.bus.MessageBus`, and `core.module.Module` enforces each module's declared
  interface at runtime. The contract is written down in [ICD.md](ICD.md).
- `app.py` is the only place that knows every module; `sim.py` feeds sample inputs.
- Diagrams: [DIAGRAMS.md](DIAGRAMS.md) (Mermaid, renders on GitHub) and `diagrams/`.

